    "insights": [
      "Threshold scales as n_k ~ (k! * d^{k-1})^{1/k} with exponent (k-1)/k",
      "Exponent (k-1)/k is non-negative, increasing, approaches 1 as k -> infinity",
      "Working with k-th power avoids fractional exponents, keeps proofs algebraic",
      "Pigeonhole (k-1)d is much larger than threshold for large d",
      "k=2 gives sqrt(2d), k=3 gives (6d^2)^{1/3}, k=4 gives (24d^3)^{1/4}"
    ],
